#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/arc4random.3:10
msgid ""
"arc4random, arc4random_uniform, arc4random_buf - cryptographically-secure "
"pseudorandom number generator"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/arc4random.3:21
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"B<uint32_t arc4random(void);>\n"
"B<uint32_t arc4random_uniform(uint32_t >I<upper_bound>B<);>\n"
"B<void arc4random_buf(>size_t n;\n"
"B<                    void >I<buf>B<[>I<n>B<], size_t >I<n>B<);>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/arc4random.3:24
msgid "These functions give cryptographically-secure pseudorandom numbers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/arc4random.3:27
msgid "B<arc4random>()  returns a uniformly-distributed value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/arc4random.3:32
msgid ""
"B<arc4random_uniform>()  returns a uniformly-distributed value less than "
"I<upper_bound> (see BUGS)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/arc4random.3:39
msgid ""
"B<arc4random_buf>()  fills the memory pointed to by I<buf>, with I<n> bytes "
"of pseudorandom data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/arc4random.3:52
msgid ""
"The B<rand>(3)  and B<drand48>(3)  families of functions should only be used "
"where the quality of the pseudorandom numbers is not a concern I<and> "
"there's a need for repeatability of the results.  Unless you meet both of "
"those conditions, use the B<arc4random>()  functions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/arc4random.3:55
msgid "B<arc4random>()  returns a pseudorandom number."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/arc4random.3:64
msgid ""
"B<arc4random_uniform>()  returns a pseudorandom number less than "
"I<upper_bound> for valid input, or B<0> when I<upper_bound> is invalid."
msgstr ""

#. type: tbl table
#: build/C/man3/arc4random.3:78
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"B<arc4random>(),\n"
"B<arc4random_uniform>(),\n"
"B<arc4random_buf>()"
msgstr ""

